{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1110849-dark-offerings-or-creative-nightmare-usage","id":1110849,"title":"Dark Offerings: Or Creative Nightmare Usage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-03T07:52:43-07:00","id":1110849,"title":"Dark Offerings: Or Creative Nightmare Usage","content":"So, I was reviewing Nightmares in the Beast book lately. Some Nightmares seem pretty straight forward, such as the ever awesomely titled Behold, My True Form! (the exclamation mark is absolutely a critical element of the title and should never be forgotten). But what of other Nightmares, such as Flying And Falling? <br /> <br /> Reading that Nightmare, I was wondering what scenario could really make it useful? Sure, there's the potential of weakening an enemy before a conflict. But making an exceptional success cost the victim a willpower point seems very... Niche? <br /> <br /> But looking at the High Satiety effect and Satiety expenditure effect... I came to the realization that this Nightmare effectively turns you into a Dark Muse on demand. Being able to afflict a person with an empowered version of Flying And Falling let's them gain exceptional successes on tasks easier. Which, for example, a Beast might find useful if that person is doing something for the Beast, like researching something or working on commissioned artwork. The High Satiety effect even allows the Beast to refuel themselves on Willpower. <br /> <br /> So, this Nightmare seems much more useful thinking of it as a support tool, rather than as a weapon. Been burning Willpower a lot lately? Commission at artist for several pieces of artwork and hit them with the Nightmare so they create stuff that's very valuable for you, meanwhile you're supping on their Willpower to recharge yourself. That artist will churn out amazing pieces of art you might be able to profit from at a later date and you'll gain strength. <br /> <br /> The cost is mentally draining your unknowing donor, but that's the cost of a muse made of nightmares, no? <br /> <br /> What other uses and combinations have people thought of for Nightmares? I'm really curious here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T14:00:21-07:00","id":1114269,"title":"","content":"Oh, I'm going to love this thread!<br /> <br /> Flying and Falling has many uses like that, there was a concept of a swimming team coach somewhere. Now, with Flying and Falling and Fear is Contagious, chances that your team will win are definetly increased! And if you feed on stuff like destroying other teams, sportman's concept of self-worth, the jealousy of other trainers etc., you can feed while doing so.<br /> <br /> You Must Obey! is another useful one, obviously.<br /> But I like They are all around you! for business-climbing Tyrants or Collectors. You want a job position, or get rid of a rival or some cop checking on your less-kosher dealings? Well, that person will have a pretty hard time convincing people of his point of view once you've driven them to the point they believe their boss has been replaced by a reptile, that a secret society of chinese delievery man is out to get them, or that money is a tool of an elite class to subjugate and subdue the people via mind-controlling agents on it.<br /> Can't remember other uses right now, but most nightmares shine outside of combat and more in social interaction and mind games. Make people believe there actually IS a monster in the cupboard, their car is cursed and needs to disappear and you are willing to get it off of them cheaply, send them into a mindless rage in the middle of a job interview, have them panick and run away when they meet their crush etc.<br /> But Wormwood, all of those are pretty mean, isn't there something nice you can do with that?<br /> Sure you can. Make Drug dealers run screaming every time they see an addict will do wonders for getting drugs out of your block, use You are alone + You cannot wake up with high sat+expenditure to make the local crime lord suffer from severe lack of authority and confidence, then use that you are basically the only one to talk to him to turn him around to a good life, and atone for his sins by handing in every piece of evidence he has in his possession. Stuff like that.<br /> <br /> Use Nightmares as a Jab, not a Cross: soften up the target, find weakspots, wear them down. Finish with your normal social/mental skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T14:06:09-07:00","id":1114272,"title":"","content":"How to terrify friends and influence people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T16:41:18-07:00","id":1115295,"title":"","content":"Hmm you know You are Lost has interesting potential to hide people. If they aren't being hunted by someone with a mystical ability to track them then wherever they're going becomes significantly harder to reach. There's a scene in Anansi Boys where Spider makes it so Fat Charlie can't get to his own home, this actually ends up at the point where he hires a cab around the corner from his apartment building and the driver can't there until they give up in the early morning. You might need to add fear is contagious for that trick, but it would be interesting. If nothing else spend Satiety and they get lost to different worlds and that'll make the tracking a pain.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T11:05:35-07:00","id":1116905,"title":"","content":"Aaaand me again. Doing more of the same. Hope you like it.<br /> <br /> So, lets look at two of &quot;fighting nightmares&quot; and their potential uses outside a fight.<br /> Don't like the Prom Queen? Hit her with All you Teeth are Falling out! during her speech. Obviously applies to everyone holding a public talk that is at least partly based on their good looks.<br /> Want another good use for this? See that asshole frat boy hitting on that girl, just not taking the hint and refusing to take a no? After this, he'll likely be no match for her.<br /> <br /> Bugs everywhere! on someone that is holding a presentation at work, sure. If youve fluffed it to be spiders, using it on arachnophobics will be more fun.<br /> But how about using it to take an arrogant Dr.Strange-type Doc down a peg, when he's at the end of the line with his knowledge and simply cannot find what is wrong with his patient?<br /> And then a nurse with a simple household treatment like cutting up an onion and putting it on gets stuff done? =D Will need You Cannot wake up, but sounds like fun.<br /> <br /> For Behold, my true Form! I see no other usage other than maybe dealing the killing blow: supernatural effects will attract enemies, but could also help build your legend. And once it is known that corrupt cops, judges, politicians, whathaveyou seem to die with seawater in their lungs/ashen white hair/ blood-red sclera/ metal spikes in their bloodstream or full on petrification, there IS going to be a Legend. Hell, even something 'boring' like a heart attack will be noticed when it crops up often enough. Death Note's Kira is a good example.<br /> <br /> Everything you do is Worthless! is awesome for sabotaging anyone, as long as you are high satiety (the normal effect needs rework imo, we have a thread about that here). But the real kicker comes in combination with Fear is Contagious and spending a lot of Satiety: you render whole groups incompetent. Sure, can be used in fights, yeah. Not as practical as the other fight-based ones, sure. But fun, and has nice uses. You want to make some money quick? Bet on a team. Get to the game. Sabotage the other team by making them fail consistently. Go to a Casino and make the cardgiver fail in manipulating the cards (still high risk, but can be lots of fun, and maybe you just want to get the cardgiver into trouble?)<br /> You suck at stealth, but need to enter a building with some guards? Guess what you can make them become horrible at?<br /> <br /> Run Away! can be nice to frame people (anyone suddenly running away from the policemen seems suspicious), make sure certain information ends up at a place you want to (high satiety, make them seek out a place or person) or make someone disappear without dirtying your hands (no bonus to resist as long as it is not overtly dangerous)<br /> <br /> High Satiety They are all around you! is simply precious in playing people, as I already mentioned above. Make someone look racist? Easy. (The [Minority Group] are in control!) Make someone look ridiculous? Done. (Chinese Delivery Man want to destroy me!) Make them ruin their career? Possibly. (Our Boss is in on it!)<br /> <br /> You are Alone! and You cannot Wake up! can easily ruin a political candidate. Especially with Satiety Expenditure. But it also helps in sabotaging Press conferences, protests, job interviews etc.<br /> Your Rival at work has an important deal coming up? Afraid he'll fumble it. Maybe he had it coming, being arrogant and convinced he can learn all he needs about a foreign culture in a day...<br /> Can also help you make friends! After all, you were the only one there to help that one time..<br /> <br /> You are not Alone! is just as versatile and evil. If not more so. How about that meeting between the emissarys, did you see how one simply refused to even look at the other? That's gonna hurt our relations with their country! Ignoring your boss, colleagues or clients can damage your career/shop etc. severely. Ignoring your wife or children can have incredible bad consequences, and crafty nemeses could surely use this to punish e.g. an unfaithful wife or arrogant children.<br /> You could, however, also use this to make someone work really, really hard and focused. Sat expenditure forces them to basically have no awareness and having to roll for perception, but they get an exceptionel success at 3. Being this super-focused will produce some fine artwork/crafted items/articles/term papers.... hell, some people might even PAY for it. Just look at what people are willing to get an edge in a super-confrontational and competitive society already. A horror trip in exchange for good grades, passing the exam, having a better chance at winning that prize... not too much of a price, right?<br /> <br /> You cannot run! can be used to make someone fail his race, sure. With decent set-up, you can make someone look completely nutty (or dangerous) for just 1 Satiety.<br /> <br /> You deserve this! is good for Nemesis forcing someone to publicly confess to their crimes, but that an easy one. Allowing people to take brutal revenge on a superior enemy might me more to your tastes.<br /> <br /> You will never rest! That's a good one! &quot;Your Co-Worker seems like he has enough on his plate as it is lately, we do not think he qualifies for this promotion. Would you like to take a shot?&quot; &quot;He used to do delicate work, but at some point he screwed up badly, and a lot of people got hurt.&quot; Anyone needing high focus on his job will utterly hate suddenly feeling tired like this. Oh, you're a ravager? combined with You cannot wake up and expending satiety/high satiety, you can initiate chaos at the airport at the very least, a catastrophe at the worst. Or just make traffic worse, if you're petty.<br /> You going for a certain doctor or pharmacist? Have some of his patients suffer from this, and make sure they get to talk to each other. Hell, you might go so far as to indicate this might be a bad side effect, malpractice even! Their greed and lawyers will do the rest. You could also spend some Satiety and make the surgeon Frightened of blood and/or sharp instruments.<br /> <br /> <br /> One Example for a set-up: Manipulating an underground match to humiliate the Boss man.<br /> Someone is proud of having the best fighters in his illegal ring? You can change that. Make sure you meet the fighters right before they go up, inflict You deserve this! on one of them, and Everything you do is worthless! on the other (have a broodmate do one of the two, so it's more inconspicious and feasible). Use Satiety. It will be a boring fight to watch, as one doesn't even attempt to block attacks, and the other constantly f*cks up. People looking for an action packed fight will be dissapointed at what will look like two bumbling idiots in an utterly boring fight. This would be bad enough publicity, but if this was to be an important betting match between fight-loving crime lords a la Ong Bak, it'll be even worse. Might even cause the typical development of mockery, offence, and infighting. Your job here is done.<br /> <br /> Just feeling I should mention this: 'With some of these, I could get the same or better results with another Nightmare!' True, possible, sure. But sometimes, you do not have another Nightmare. You make do with what you have. And for that, I like being able to apply the skills more creatively.<br /> I remember a thread about creative use of Arcana, and when I pointed out you could enhance your perception of time with Life, and thus your reaction speed (if not your movement speed), someone else complained that you could do the same more easily with Time.<br /> What if my character does not HAVE Time, since he's a Druid-Medic with a Focus on Life and Mind? Well, he'll be happy to make the most of what he has, and you don't always have a teammate around to do the stuff you cannot do (hey, they might be busy, or have enough on their platter already!). I hope you'll find that you agree.<br /> <br /> <br /> Will be looking into some of the non-common Nightmares later, but I already find myself agreeing with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3400_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3400\" data-vbnamecard=\"3400\">nalak42</a> 's approach to You are Lost!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 07-16-2017, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}